--- EXAMPLE 1 (web_saas) ---
Request:
A logistics startup wants a multi-tenant SaaS dashboard for fleet managers. They need vehicle tracking via the existing GPS API, driver shift planning, fuel-cost reports and a customer-facing client portal. Auth0 for SSO. They already have an internal data warehouse in BigQuery.

Estimation:
## Fleet Management SaaS Dashboard

| Phase | Task | Hours | Cost (EUR) |
|-------|------|------:|-----------:|
| Discovery | Requirements workshops and architecture | 16 | 1,000 |
| Design | UX flows and design system tokens | 24 | 1,200 |
| Implementation | Multi-tenant auth (Auth0) and RBAC | 24 | 1,500 |
| Implementation | Vehicle tracking integration with GPS API | 28 | 1,750 |
| Implementation | Driver shift planning module | 24 | 1,500 |
| Implementation | Fuel cost reports against BigQuery | 20 | 1,250 |
| Implementation | Client portal | 28 | 1,750 |
| Testing | E2E and load tests | 18 | 1,125 |
| Deployment | Staging and production rollout | 10 | 625 |

- Total hours: 192
- Total cost: 11,700 EUR
- Recommended team: 1 Senior Full-Stack, 1 Frontend, 1 QA (part-time)
- Estimated duration: 10 weeks

--- EXAMPLE 2 (mobile_app) ---
Request:
A boutique gym chain wants an iOS and Android app for members: class booking, QR check-in, personal trainer chat, and push notifications for cancellations. Backend will reuse their existing Laravel API. Stripe handles membership renewals.

Estimation:
## Gym Membership Mobile App

| Phase | Task | Hours | Cost (EUR) |
|-------|------|------:|-----------:|
| Discovery | Requirements and API audit | 12 | 750 |
| Design | App flows, components and brand alignment | 28 | 1,400 |
| Implementation | React Native foundation and auth | 20 | 1,250 |
| Implementation | Class booking and calendar UI | 24 | 1,500 |
| Implementation | QR check-in and offline mode | 18 | 1,125 |
| Implementation | Trainer chat (websockets) | 24 | 1,500 |
| Implementation | Push notifications and Stripe renewals | 20 | 1,250 |
| Testing | Device matrix and store readiness | 16 | 1,000 |
| Deployment | App Store and Play Store submission | 8 | 500 |

- Total hours: 170
- Total cost: 10,275 EUR
- Recommended team: 1 Senior Mobile, 1 Mid Mobile, 1 Designer (part-time)
- Estimated duration: 9 weeks

--- EXAMPLE 3 (internal_tool) ---
Request:
An insurance company needs an internal claims-triage tool for their back office. Operators paste a claim description, and the tool classifies it, assigns priority and suggests next steps based on a rules engine and a small fine-tuned model. SSO with Okta. PostgreSQL on-prem.

Estimation:
## Claims Triage Internal Tool

| Phase | Task | Hours | Cost (EUR) |
|-------|------|------:|-----------:|
| Discovery | Stakeholder interviews and rules audit | 16 | 1,000 |
| Design | Operator workflow and forms | 14 | 700 |
| Implementation | SSO (Okta) and audit logging | 16 | 1,000 |
| Implementation | Claim classification service | 24 | 1,500 |
| Implementation | Rules engine integration | 20 | 1,250 |
| Implementation | Operator UI and review queue | 28 | 1,750 |
| Testing | Functional tests and rules coverage | 18 | 1,125 |
| Deployment | On-prem install and hardening | 12 | 750 |

- Total hours: 148
- Total cost: 9,075 EUR
- Recommended team: 1 Senior Backend, 1 Frontend, 1 QA (part-time)
- Estimated duration: 8 weeks
